From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The bag in the lower menu's panel (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Where the 3DS remaster can show its lower menu, the bag shows in the
menu's panel, as its approved tall mock-up has it (2026-10-24): its main
screen (the list, the pockets, the description) on the lower screen (the
DS's screen swap), laid out 248 lines tall:

- the list's box 7 tile rows longer (its middle row again) and the list
  3 lines longer (12, BAG_UI_NUM_VISIBLE_ITEMS);
- below the list, 7 rows lower: the pockets' panel, the description bar,
  and the windows and sprites with them (the item's menu, the messages,
  the counts and their arrows, the item's icon and its box, a TM's type
  and category);
- above the pockets, the bag 1.25 times as big (its affine matrix),
  drawn smoothly by the port, its shadow two tiles wider under it.

The list's window is taller, so BG2 has its tiles in a block of their own
(0x18000), the pocket names' after the list's; BG0's windows keep theirs.
The sprite system's main screen goes on to line 255 meanwhile
(SpriteUtil_PortTallMainScreen: the sub screen's sprites from 256).

The bag's touch screen isn't shown, so the panel's touches are nobody's.
The upper screen keeps the field.

Opened from the menu, the bag comes like a window brought back, not a
program started: no fade in, none out when B (or CLOSE BAG) puts it away.
Both screens keep what they show while the field goes and the bag comes
(the menu with BAG lit), and the other way round; the bag shows whole two
frames after it's there, the field three, the menu still open on BAG.

While the item list waits, the menu's other buttons work, with the tap's
sound: BAG puts the bag away and closes the menu; POKéMON, TRAINER,
POKéDEX and OPTIONS open straight from the bag (both screens black at
once, as the field's fade out leaves them, then the app's fade in); SAVE,
MAP and POKéTCH are acted on back in the field. A tap while the bag's busy
(an item's menu, a message) is nobody's. The bag hands the button to the
start menu (gStartMenuPortAppPress): the menu forgets its press when it
goes off.

Leaving another way (an item used, given) is the DS's fade out, the upper
screen kept till the game's picture there is as bright as what was kept;
the bag opened again after that comes with fades too, and the menu's
buttons close it with one. The bag puts everything back when it ends.
Without the menu (--classic-menu, or a platform that can't show it) the
bag is as before, across the wider upper screen.
